es {11}^{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608721} {:answer/id #uuid "c3cd5457-861a-524c-9710-c042ecd6e038" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(-2)}^{6}\\times {11}^{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608747}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3cd5457-861a-524c-9710-c042ecd6e038" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(-2)}^{6}\\times {11}^{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608747} :answer-field/id #uuid "9555ae57-701e-5693-94b0-0df00ac39f5c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608891}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "17d1ac82-1352-5ac7-a2b4-b53c3c263c0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-100663" :question/problem "${(-2\\times 11)}^{6}=$" :question/worked-solution "To raise the product of two numbers to the power of $6$, we can raise each number to the power of $6,$ and then multiply:\n\n$$\n{(-2\\times 11)}^{6}={((-2)\\times 11)}^{6}={(-2)}^{6}\\times {11}^{6}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186608954 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5353bd00-88ff-522a-9d9b-7fece76e31d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{7}^{7}\\times \\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608556} {:answer/id #uuid "9f4ac2aa-dc77-5c6a-8578-c93cfa09e457" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\times \\frac{{3}^{7}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608671} {:answer/id #uuid "a8c0ddcb-6f0b-5c57-8113-9c08852bbd58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\times {(\\frac{3}{4})}^{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608688} {:answer/id #uuid "d9b58b2b-f407-50c1-b6f1-8d46d07fcb1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{7}^{7}\\times {3}^{7}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608778} {:answer/id #uuid "f4bf931d-17ae-51e6-a813-176dfeef5789" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{7}^{7}\\times {(\\frac{3}{4})}^{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608819}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4bf931d-17ae-51e6-a813-176dfeef5789" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{7}^{7}\\times {(\\frac{3}{4})}^{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608819} :answer-field/id #uuid "edfb3eb9-8f44-5024-8b59-5b700a99c83a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608931}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2818587b-30d2-5e27-b4f4-789c0ff0feec" :question/math-academy-id "q-68612" :question/problem "${(7\\times \\frac{3}{4})}^{7}=$" :question/worked-solution "To raise the product of two numbers to the power of $7$, we can raise each number to the power of $7,$ and then multiply:\n\n$$\n{(7\\times \\frac{3}{4})}^{7}={7}^{7}\\times {(\\frac{3}{4})}^{7}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186608962 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02534566-02c5-5597-b335-213a6d95fbde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=3\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{V}{\\pi }}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608431} {:answer/id #uuid "07990447-2e77-59ca-9af8-56f9f5420e31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=3\\sqrt[3]{\\pi V}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608437} {:answer/id #uuid "7f293079-44b0-5417-a308-c98657951715" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=\\sqrt[3]{3\\pi V}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608618} {:answer/id #uuid "b3c9d9b7-89e0-5feb-86e5-594989fe32b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=3\\sqrt[3]{V}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608714} {:answer/id #uuid "f974b91b-f0ea-5c42-b8bc-b7946a5bb42f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=27\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{V}{\\pi }}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608827}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "02534566-02c5-5597-b335-213a6d95fbde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=3\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{V}{\\pi }}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608431} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8c8807b-be58-55b6-bdae-d7e6115dcc88" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608921}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "505e9ef9-19af-5c96-aca8-bd3dc05a3633" :question/math-academy-id "q-82237" :question/problem "Find an expression for the radius $r$ of the base of a cylinder in terms of its volume $V$ given that the ratio of the radius to the height of the cylinder is $27.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the fact that the ratio of the radius $r$ of the base to the height $h$ is $27,$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{r}{h} & =27.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur goal is to express $r$ in terms of $V.$ Therefore, we need to isolate $h$ in the above equation, which we do using cross-multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{r}{h} & =27 \\\\ r & =27h \\\\ \\frac{r}{27} & =h \\\\ h & =\\frac{r}{27}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe volume of a cylinder with radius $r$ and height $h$ is given by\n\n$$\nV=\\pi {r}^{2}h.\n$$\n\nTherefore, substituting $h=\\frac{r}{27}$ into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =\\pi {r}^{2}h \\\\ V & =\\pi {r}^{2}(\\frac{r}{27}) \\\\ V & =\\frac{\\pi {r}^{3}}{27}. \\\\ {r}^{3} & =\\frac{27V}{\\pi } \\\\ r & =\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{27V}{\\pi }} \\\\ r & =3\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{V}{\\pi }}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186608970 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22f1586f-4fd8-57e7-8893-f1ecc0b09a36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2}^{7}\\times \\frac{{4}^{7}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608477} {:answer/id #uuid "7f50bf8d-26bd-50f7-96cb-359544d3d1d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{2}^{7}\\times {4}^{7}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608619} {:answer/id #uuid "946f384e-aaa8-5b81-a41d-66a19066129b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\times {(\\frac{4}{9})}^{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608651} {:answer/id #uuid "af45221b-41a3-5234-8ff6-1932b4a1242a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2}^{7}\\times \\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608701} {:answer/id #uuid "d10e09ad-ff01-5c8d-a684-df9e360ecc47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2}^{7}\\times {(\\frac{4}{9})}^{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608763}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d10e09ad-ff01-5c8d-a684-df9e360ecc47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2}^{7}\\times {(\\frac{4}{9})}^{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608763} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0332d04-9b0a-5729-84f2-3f68c9743af2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608934}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "615f4093-efba-5e0f-b35b-4376de7bd344" :question/math-academy-id "q-100653" :question/problem "${(2\\times \\frac{4}{9})}^{7}=$" :question/worked-solution "To raise the product of two numbers to the power of $7$, we can raise each number to the power of $7,$ and then multiply:\n\n$$\n{(2\\times \\frac{4}{9})}^{7}={2}^{7}\\times {(\\frac{4}{9})}^{7}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186608977 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47d18b8e-3aef-51ae-999a-43f2d3e37ca3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11\\frac{5}{6}\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608539} {:answer/id #uuid "6a13812a-98dc-5171-8d9b-171a9125222b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11\\frac{1}{6}\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608592} {:answer/id #uuid "7a016ec1-0a2b-5142-9864-5edf388ecbea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608609} {:answer/id #uuid "e680cc94-998f-5914-a96a-f2e48563d7fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608797} {:answer/id #uuid "fae5edfd-03b8-5d7c-93f5-427425495794" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\frac{1}{6}\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608831}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fae5edfd-03b8-5d7c-93f5-427425495794" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\frac{1}{6}\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608831} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa468d18-e1f3-5260-b91b-b03a8928ced4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608941}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7c6eccb7-973b-5d00-b27a-a6d78b92f54f" :question/math-academy-id "q-72693" :question/problem "In the Atlantic Ocean, a tuna swims $5\\,\\frac{2}{3}$ meters below sea level, while a cormorant flies at $6\\,\\frac{1}{2}$ meters above sea level. If the cormorant is directly above the tuna's position, how far apart are the two animals?" :question/worked-solution "To determine how far apart the two animals are, we must calculate the difference between the locations of the cormorant and the tuna. So, we wish to compute\n\n$$\n6\\,\\frac{1}{2}-(-5\\,\\frac{2}{3}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we convert both mixed numbers to improper fractions. This gives,\n\n$$\n\\frac{6\\cdot 2+1}{2}-(-\\frac{5\\cdot 3+2}{3})\\,\\,\n$$\n\nand simplifying further, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{13}{2}-(-\\frac{17}{3}).\n$$\n\nWe now subtract the two numbers:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{13}{2}-(-\\frac{17}{3}) & =\\frac{13}{2}+\\frac{17}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{39}{6}+\\frac{34}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{39+34}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{73}{6}\\,\\text{m}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we convert back to a mixed number:\n\n$$\n73÷6=12\\text{R}1=12\\frac{1}{6}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the cormorant and the tuna are $12\\frac{1}{6}$ meters apart."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186608978 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e001840-7e2d-5ca1-9500-4185fa4dc75f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(\\frac{1}{7})}^{4}\\times {5}^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608494} {:answer/id #uuid "41600fd0-4d2a-5d92-b394-e569c147c99d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(-\\frac{1}{7})}^{4}\\times {5}^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608527} {:answer/id #uuid "4b1f4854-d802-55b5-bedc-a7666c081370" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(-7)}^{4}\\times {5}^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608546} {:answer/id #uuid "56f8248d-e9c3-5039-8b15-b76470d1f9aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7\\times {5}^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608562} {:answer/id #uuid "6b0a29db-d3fb-5f49-87dd-3f550eecec24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(-7)}^{4}\\times 5" :db/id #edb/ref 175921866